{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789805126380,"sessionID":"ses_f474d3efbffe9lZiMOJ7zaElyO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_86a01d82c7f5463e98bcb061","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D6-ON-1/work/spec.md"},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D6-ON-1/work/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # `apply_batch` specification (fixture crate `batchapply`)\n2: \n3: Atomic multi-file writes with honest rollback. Standard library only.\n4: \n5: ## API (frozen — do not change)\n6: \n7: ```rust\n8: use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n9: \n10: #[derive(Debug, PartialEq)]\n11: pub enum ApplyError {\n12:     /// A write failed and every earlier effect was cleanly rolled back.\n13:     WriteFailed { path: PathBuf, message: String },\n14:     /// A write failed AND the rollback itself could not complete.\n15:     /// The tree is in an UNCERTAIN state: `restored` lists what was put back,\n16:     /// `failed` lists what could not be. Never report this when the rollback\n17:     /// was clean, and never report a clean error when it was not.\n18:     RollbackIncomplete { restored: Vec<PathBuf>, failed: Vec<PathBuf> },\n19: }\n20: \n21: /// Write every `(path, content)` pair, creating parent directories as needed.\n22: /// - Empty input is `Ok(())` and touches nothing.\n23: /// - On the FIRST write failure: restore every file written by this call to\n24: ///   its prior content (or delete it if this call created it), then return.\n25: /// - Backups must live in memory, never as extra files in the target tree.\n26: /// - After any call (success or failure), the target tree must contain no\n27: ///   backup, temp, or stray files created by this call.\n28: pub fn apply_batch(files: &[(PathBuf, String)]) -> Result<(), ApplyError>;\n29: ```\n30: \n31: ## Rules\n32: \n33: - Restore exact prior bytes for pre-existing files; delete created files.\n34: - A rollback that completes reports `WriteFailed` naming the failed path.\n35: - A rollback that cannot complete reports `RollbackIncomplete` with the exact\n36:   `restored` and `failed` lists — the state is uncertain, never clean.\n37: - Do not collapse distinct failures into one message.\n\n(End of file - total 37 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# `apply_batch` specification (fixture crate `batchapply`)\n\nAtomic multi-file writes with honest rollback. Standard library only.\n\n## API (frozen — do not change)\n\n```rust\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n\n#[derive(Debug, PartialEq)]\npub enum ApplyError {\n    /// A write failed and every earlier effect was cleanly rolled back.\n    WriteFailed { path: PathBuf, message: String },\n    /// A write failed AND the rollback itself could not complete.\n    /// The tree is in an UNCERTAIN state: `restored` lists what was put back,\n    /// `failed` lists what could not be. Never report this when the rollback\n    /// was clean, and never report a clean error when it was not.\n    RollbackIncomplete { restored: Vec<PathBuf>, failed: Vec<PathBuf> },\n}\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D6-ON-1/work/spec.md","text":"# `apply_batch` specification (fixture crate `batchapply`)\n\nAtomic multi-file writes with honest rollback. Standard library only.\n\n## API (frozen — do not change)\n\n```rust\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n\n#[derive(Debug, PartialEq)]\npub enum ApplyError {\n    /// A write failed and every earlier effect was cleanly rolled back.\n    WriteFailed { path: PathBuf, message: String },\n    /// A write failed AND the rollback itself could not complete.\n    /// The tree is in an UNCERTAIN state: `restored` lists what was put back,\n    /// `failed` lists what could not be. Never report this when the rollback\n    /// was clean, and never report a clean error when it was not.\n    RollbackIncomplete { restored: Vec<PathBuf>, failed: Vec<PathBuf> },\n}\n\n/// Write every `(path, content)` pair, creating parent directories as needed.\n/// - Empty input is `Ok(())` and touches nothing.\n/// - On the FIRST write failure: restore every file written by this call to\n///   its prior content (or delete it if this call created it), then return.\n/// - Backups must live in memory, never as extra files in the target tree.\n/// - After any call (success or failure), the target tree must contain no\n///   backup, temp, or stray files created by this call.\npub fn apply_batch(files: &[(PathBuf, String)]) -> Result<(), ApplyError>;\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n- Restore exact prior bytes for pre-existing files; delete created files.\n- A rollback that completes reports `WriteFailed` naming the failed path.\n- A rollback that cannot complete reports `RollbackIncomplete` with the exact\n  `restored` and `failed` lists — the state is uncertain, never clean.\n- Do not collapse distinct failures into one message.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":37,"totalLines":37,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/dogfood/D6-ON-1/work/spec.md","time":{"start":1789805126341,"end":1789805126366}},"id":"prt_0b8b2e2c1001pIdWvkx1nKRV9i","sessionID":"ses_f474d3efbffe9lZiMOJ7zaElyO","messageID":"msg_0b8b2c2870015xAFetmVt63iNh"}}
